# llm-guard.baseline — exceptions for scripts/llm-guard.py, each VERIFIED BY HAND.
#
# Format:  <doc>  TAB  <key>  TAB  <why this finding is not a defect>
#   key = <cited-path>:<lo>-<hi>   for a `citations` finding
#         symbol:<name>            for a `symbols` finding whose name belongs to another repo
#
# Only `citations` and cross-repo `symbols` findings can be listed here. `paths`, `forbidden`,
# `phantom`, `version`, out-of-bounds and `vacuous` are deterministic and always fail.
#
# The key carries the CITED coordinates (or the symbol name) on purpose: a citation that later
# drifts to a different line stops matching its entry and the gate fires.  An entry matching
# nothing is reported as `baseline-stale` and FAILS, so this file cannot rot into a blanket
# exemption.  Re-derive with: python3 scripts/llm-guard.py --no-baseline
#
# The `symbol:` entries are names that belong to qb, not to qbm-redis: this repo's CI checks
# out only this repo, so they cannot be resolved here.  Nothing is lost overall — the qb-dev
# superproject's dev/agent/llm-guard.py sees both trees and verifies them for real.  This file
# states which names are taken on trust, by name, rather than letting them pass silently.

llm/qbm-redis.llm.api.md	symbol:qb_load_modules	qb's own CMake function, defined in qb/cmake/qbFunctions.cmake (and re-exported by qb/cmake/qbConfig.cmake).
llm/qbm-redis.llm.md	symbol:init	`qb::io::async::init()` — qb-io's per-thread loop initialiser, qb/src/qb/io/async/listener.h:1542. The sentence names it as the thing to call once from synchronous code.
llm/qbm-redis.llm.md	symbol:run_sync	`qb::io::async::run_sync(...)` — qb-io's synchronous pump, qb/src/qb/io/async/coroutine/utils.h:293. Named in the same sentence, for the same reason.
llm/qbm-redis.llm.api.md	symbol:with_multiplier	A builder of `qb::io::reconnect_policy`, the struct `qb::redis::RetryPolicy` aliases since Huly QB-126 -- declared in qb/src/qb/io/reconnect.h, not in this repo.
llm/qbm-redis.llm.api.md	symbol:with_jitter	A builder of `qb::io::reconnect_policy`, the struct `qb::redis::RetryPolicy` aliases since Huly QB-126 -- declared in qb/src/qb/io/reconnect.h, not in this repo.
llm/qbm-redis.llm.api.md	symbol:with_on_retry	A builder of `qb::io::reconnect_policy`, the struct `qb::redis::RetryPolicy` aliases since Huly QB-126 -- declared in qb/src/qb/io/reconnect.h, not in this repo.

# The one below is the content rule inferring a citation's subject from the nearest
# backticked word where that word is not the subject.  The citation is correct.
#
# It used to be three.  The other two -- the connector class and `struct score` -- are gone
# because the citations they excused were WIDENED to hold their own subject rather than
# baselined around it: the connector heading's citation runs from the class template through
# the state members the sentence lists (`_uri`, `std::optional<RetryPolicy> _reconnect_policy`,
# the connection state, `_verify_peer`, the `_alive` liveness token -- read the current span in
# llm/qbm-redis.llm.api.md), and the score row's from `struct score` through `struct score_member`.
# (The lines these notes once carried were true when written and drifted after: a note is not a
# citation, so nothing moved it.)
# Note what the deleted rationales asserted: they placed `struct score` and `score_member` each
# one line low when they were written, so the prose that justified the exception was itself
# mis-citing the header.  Nothing gates that prose; read it
# against the source before trusting it, and re-derive it whenever an entry moves.
llm/qbm-redis.llm.api.md	redis.h:1535-1535	correct: `class Redis` is qbm/redis/src/qbm/redis/redis.h:1535. The citation opens the line, so it has no preceding subject and the rule falls back to `*_commands` prose.
